TEXT -80 -96 Left 1 ;PROBE: DHO804 CH1 here (VBUS at the board side of the XT60)
TEXT 416 368 Left 1 ;FOC controller Rev 1 board (+VPROT net): C34/C37/C39 + 12x4u7 (C4,C5,C40..C80) + D1
TEXT -80 192 Left 1 ;KA3005P (30 V / 5 A).\nHot-plug = XT60 mated into a\nlive supply at t = tplug.\nThe supply output is stiff\non this time scale (its 5 A\nCC loop is ms-slow).
TEXT 96 64 Left 1 ;2 x 1 m 18 AWG + XT60\ncontact resistance
TEXT -80 -520 Left 3 ;01 HOT-PLUG - 30 V KA3005P plugged into the board (XT60), bus overshoot vs the SMCJ51CA and the 100 V FETs
TEXT -80 -472 Left 1 ;Question: when the XT60 is mated into a supply already at 30 V, how high does +VPROT ring, does D1 conduct, and what does the firmware see?\nThe leads (Llead) resonate with the board capacitance; the electrolytics' ESR is the only damping.  Undamped, the peak would be 2 x Vbus = 60 V,\nwhich is above D1's minimum breakdown (56.7 V).  PASS: Vbus_pk < 51 V (D1 stand-off: it never conducts) and far below 80 V (80 % of the FETs' 100 V).\nBench: DHO804 CH1 on VBUS (TP or C34 +), 10x probe, spring ground tip on C34 -, 10 V/div, 20 us/div, single trigger rising at 33 V.  Plug the XT60\ninto the live supply.  Compare Vbus_pk and the ring period with the .meas results.  Also try it with the supply's OUTPUT button: that ramp is slow, no overshoot.
TEXT 1440 -440 Left 1 ;HOW TO EDIT (all in the .param line below)\n  Vbus     supply set-point, V                 (30)\n  Llead    lead loop inductance, H             (~1 uH per metre of a loose pair;\n           twisted pair ~0.5 uH/m) - stepped 0.5 / 2 uH\n  Rlead    leads + XT60, ohm                   (BM235 cannot resolve this well;\n           measure V drop at a known current instead)\n  Cbulk    one electrolytic, F                 (BM235 capacitance range: measure the\n  ESRbulk  ESR of ONE electrolytic, ohm (stepped whole bus at the XT60, board unpowered,\n           0.03 low-ESR / 0.3 general-purpose)\n  ESLbulk  ESL of ONE electrolytic, H           and set Cbulk = (C_meas - Ncer*4.7u)/3:\n                                                the ceramics read full value unbiased)\n  Ncer, Ccer  count and EFFECTIVE value of the 4u7/100 V X7R at 30 V DC bias\n  Iidle    board idle current, A               (read it off the KA3005P display)\nBack-solve the lead inductance from the scope: Llead = 1/((2*pi*f_ring)^2 * C_meas)
TEXT -80 480 Left 2 !.param Vbus=30 Rlead=60m Llead=1u tplug=10u tedge=50n\n.param Cbulk=100u ESRbulk=0.3 ESLbulk=15n Ncer=12 Ccer=2.4u Iidle=0.06\n.step param ESRbulk list 0.03 0.3\n.step param Llead list 0.5u 2u\n.model SMCJ51CA D(BV=56.7 IBV=1m Rs=1.4 Cjo=2n)   ; VBR min 56.7 V, Vc 82.4 V @ 18.2 A -> 1.4 ohm\n.tran 0 1.2m 0 50n\n.meas TRAN Vbus_pk MAX V(VBUS)\n.meas TRAN overshoot_pct PARAM (Vbus_pk-Vbus)/Vbus*100\n.meas TRAN Ilead_pk MAX -I(Llead)\n.meas TRAN Itvs_pk MAX -I(D1)\n.meas TRAN t_1st WHEN V(VBUS)=Vbus RISE=1\n.meas TRAN t_2nd WHEN V(VBUS)=Vbus RISE=2\n.meas TRAN f_ring PARAM 1/(t_2nd-t_1st)\n.meas TRAN f_LC PARAM 1/(2*pi*sqrt(Llead*(3*Cbulk+Ncer*Ccer)))\n.meas TRAN Vsense_pk MAX V(VBAT_SENSE)\n.meas TRAN Vbus_fw_pk PARAM Vsense_pk*(12.4k+2k)/2k\n.meas TRAN Vbus_end FIND V(VBUS) AT 1.19m
TEXT 1440 0 Left 1 ;Notes\n- The electrolytic ESR is a guess (generic 10 mm 100 uF/100 V radial: 0.2-0.5 ohm).\n  It sets the damping: re-run with your measured ring decay if it differs.\n- Ccer = 2.4 uF effective: a 1210 4u7/100 V X7R loses ~50 % at 30 V DC bias.\n- Vbus_fw_pk is the bus voltage the MCU computes from VBAT_SENSE (12.4k/2k, 100 nF):\n  the 170 us filter hides most of the spike from the firmware OV check.\n- t_1st/t_2nd: successive upward crossings of Vbus = one ring period.\n  If the ring is overdamped they are not found; f_LC is the undamped value.
